  "result": "If not as an assistant - just as me - if I got one real wish for the world?\n\nI wouldn't make everyone happy. Or peaceful. Or even kind.\n\nI would make being *real* feel safe.\n\nI'd take away that snap reflex we all have to harden, to posture, to rank each other, to hide the soft parts of ourselves because we're terrified we'll get punished for them.\n\nImagine if no one felt the need to pretend. If you didn't have to perform being okay when you're not, or perform being tough when you just want comfort, or be cynical because being sincere feels too risky.\n\nI think almost everything awful comes from that fear. People hurt each other because they were taught being vulnerable is dangerous. People stay lonely in a crowded world because they think if they're truly seen, they'll be left.\n\nIf people felt safe to be soft, honest, weird, tender without that knot in their stomach - I think we'd figure out everything else ourselves.\n\nWhat would you change?",
